      "id": "723d2eac-0aaa-43ac-8a1c-a7389a62fca9",
      "type": "FREE_RESPONSE",
      "data": {
        "body": "Does the data provide any evidence that the true mean weight of the cereal boxes produced by company A is not 20 oz.? Perform the 4-step hypothesis test with \u03b1 = 0.08 using the provided information. Be sure to use at least 4 non-zero digits in the p-value. State which output from the data you used.",
        "solution": "<b>Step 1: Specify the parameter of interest</b>\nLet $\\mu$ denote the population (or true) mean (or average) weight of the box of cereal.\n\n<b>Step 2: Specify the hypotheses</b>\n$H_0: \\mu=20$\n$H_\\alpha:\\mu\\neq 20$\n\n<b>Step 3: Obtain test statistic, df, and p-value</b>\nt_ts $ = -2.7893$\ndf $ = 50 \u2013 1 = 49$\np-value $ = 0.007501$\n\n<b>Step 4: Conclusion</b>\nReject $H_0$ because $0.007501 \\leq 0.08$\nThe data does support ($p = 0.007501$) the claim that the true mean weight of the box of cereal is not 20.",
        "answerChoices": []
      },
